cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. The bundled SMAP/MSL example preserves the upstream finding that the success criterion was not met; synthetic examples are labelled SYNTHETIC."
title: "Evidence Passport: offline MVP that turns one experiment-run manifest into a static HTML evidence passport and normalized JSON"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/evidence-passport"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
abstract: >-
  Offline, Python-standard-library MVP that validates a single experiment-run
  manifest and writes a static HTML evidence passport plus normalized JSON.
  It records declared project, dataset, code, protocol, seed, baseline, metric,
  limitation, and artifact details with fail-closed SHA-256 checks. It does not
  generate data, score signals, or combine metrics. Bundled examples include an
  OES-Resilience NASA SMAP/MSL public-dataset passport where the preregistered
  success criterion was not met, and three SYNTHETIC examples. Not a validation
  authority, provenance service, clinical device, or hardware product.
keywords:
  - evidence
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - audit
  - offline
  - synthetic data
  - open science
